---LINES
#ok	= gv - - - - "[ ok ]"
ok	= gh - - - - "[ ok ]"
err	= ge - - - - "[ exit= 1 ]"






---SCREEN
=command run & exit trap

  When command is done, You will receive the indicator in the form below:

  .ok...       - execution completed without errors

  .err........ - execution terminated with an error or on a signal


  Switch context pressing a key:
  
  .:SP... or .:CA...      - return to main menu
  .:HE...                 - get this page then returns to main menu
  .:AU... .:AD... .:AR... - return to command editor, cursor at the end 
  .:AL...                 - return to command editor, cursor at last position
  .'any_printable         - type another command from scratch

  Note about protective trap:
    pressing .:NL... does nothing preventing unexpected action

---END
